Subject: vmwarefusion: suspend the VM hard, never soft

A soft suspend runs the guest's VMware Tools network script, which on boot2docker flushes the
address from eth0, docker0 and every container's interface, and on resume only sets them up again:
no DHCP, no docker0 address, since boot2docker has none of the network services the script looks
for. The VM resumes running but unreachable (spike, 2026-11-24). That is what Wowfunhappy's
suspend.disabled = "TRUE" avoided ("disables suspend in vmware because that screws up stuff").

A hard suspend skips the guest scripts, and the VM resumes with everything intact: same IP, docker0,
the /Users share, a synced clock and running containers. Suspend itself must stay allowed: VMware
hot-adds memory and CPUs to a running VM by a suspend-and-resume, and suspend.disabled makes that
silently do nothing. Payload's harden_suspend makes the same change to a VM created before this.

--- a/drivers/vmwarefusion/vmx_darwin.go
+++ b/drivers/vmwarefusion/vmx_darwin.go
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@
 powerType.powerOff = "soft"
 powerType.powerOn = "soft"
 powerType.reset = "soft"
-powerType.suspend = "soft"
+powerType.suspend = "hard"
 scsi0.present = "TRUE"
 scsi0.virtualDev = "pvscsi"
 scsi0:0.fileName = "{{.MachineName}}.vmdk"
